## Review specialists

`/review` and `/build` pick specialist reviewers by the paths a change touches.

| Changed paths | Role file |
| --- | --- |
| `apps/backend/**` (including its `infra/` and `template.yaml`), `infra/**` | `.claude/roles/review/backend.md` |
| `apps/frontend/**`, `packages/shared/**` | `.claude/roles/review/frontend.md` |
| `packages/ui-kit/**` | `.claude/roles/review/ui-kit.md` |
| `docs/**`, `**/*.md` | `.claude/roles/review/docs.md` |

When two or more specialists apply, the lead reviewer (`review-lead`) also reviews the
cross-cutting concerns.

## Personas

The people who use the product. Planning uses these names as the persona on every
story. Replace the examples with the real ones.

| Persona | Who they are |
| --- | --- |
| `admin` | Manages the product and its users (Cognito group `admin`) |
| `user` | A signed-in person using the product |
| `visitor` | Someone who isn't signed in |
| `developer` | Someone changing the code (for internal stories only) |

## Decisions agents must check

Changes are checked against the numbered invariants in every `Accepted` record in
`docs/decisions/` (the `decision-checker` subagent does this).
